WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.600
Pytest.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:05.077
Every serious Python AI repo you'll touch runs it.

3
00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:05.967
Let's see why.

4
00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.433
Pytest is the de facto test runner.

5
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:14.367
You write plain assert statements, and pytest shows you both sides when one fails.

6
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.167
It discovers every test file automatically.

7
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.500
Fixtures declare shared setup once.

8
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.033
And parametrize runs one test over many cases.

9
00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.633
Here's how fixtures work.

10
00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:29.367
You declare the setup once, in a function marked as a fixture.

11
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.867
Any test that names it as a parameter...

12
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.356
receives the value automatically.

13
00:00:34.356 --> 00:00:39.000
Fixtures can be composed and scoped to a function, module, or session.

14
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.467
Parametrize turns a table of inputs into separate tests.

15
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.633
The first row: a zero diameter scores zero.

16
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:49.833
The second: a big, close asteroid scores high.

17
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:53.495
The third: tiny and far away scores almost nothing.

18
00:00:53.495 --> 00:00:55.933
Each row is reported as its own case.

19
00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:58.033
And in code.

20
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:01.767
The fixture returns a close approach for the asteroid Apophis.

21
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:05.033
The test simply names it as a parameter, and gets it.

22
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:10.933
Parametrize runs one body over every input and expected pair, using approx for floats.

23
00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.100
A real case.

24
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.633
Your RAG regression suite is one parametrized test over forty golden questions.

25
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:22.167
CI runs it after every prompt or chunking change.

26
00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:28.520
A failure names the exact question that regressed, instead of a vague note that the eval got worse.

27
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.167
Fixtures hold a mocked vector store, so nothing touches live infrastructure.

28
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.139
Let's recap.

29
00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:39.067
Pytest uses plain asserts and finds your tests automatically.

30
00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.067
Fixtures share setup by name.

31
00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.433
Parametrize runs one body over many cases.

32
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:49.012
Built-ins like monkeypatch and tmp path cover most mocking.

33
00:01:49.012 --> 00:01:50.100
Next up: NumPy.
